.TH RASPIBACKUP.CONF 5 "@DATE@" "raspiBackup @VERSION@" "raspiBackup Manual"
.SH NAME
raspiBackup.conf \- configuration file for raspiBackup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
.br
.I ~/.raspiBackup.conf
.br
.I ./.raspiBackup.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR raspiBackup (1)
reads its defaults from up to three configuration files, in this order:
.IP 1. 4
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
(system wide)
.IP 2. 4
.I ~/.raspiBackup.conf
(home directory of the calling user)
.IP 3. 4
.I ./.raspiBackup.conf
(current directory)
.PP
followed by the file passed with
.BR \-f .
Settings of a later file override earlier ones, and command line options
override all of them.
.PP
The files are sourced by
.BR bash (1).
Each line has the form
.IP
.IB NAME = value
.PP
without spaces around
.BR = .
Values containing spaces have to be quoted.
Lines starting with
.B #
are comments.
Boolean options use
.B 0
for off and
.B 1
for on.
.PP
When the Debian package is installed and no system wide configuration
exists, it is created from the template matching the system language in
.IR /usr/local/share/raspibackup .
The configuration is never overwritten by a package update; use
.B raspiBackup \-\-updateConfig
to merge options of a new release into an existing configuration.
.BR raspiBackupInstallUI (1)
edits the most important options interactively.
.PP
.B VERSION_CONFIG
holds the version of the configuration file format and must not be
changed.
.PP
The command line option corresponding to a setting is shown in brackets.
.SH BACKUP OPTIONS
.TP
.B DEFAULT_BACKUPPATH
Directory where backups are stored.
A partition (local or remote) should be mounted there.
Default: /backup.
.RB [ \-p ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_BACKUPTYPE
.BR dd ,
.B tar
or
.BR rsync .
Default: rsync.
.RB [ \-t ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_ZIP_BACKUP
Compress dd and tar backups.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-z ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_DD_BACKUP_SAVE_USED_PARTITIONS_ONLY
dd backups save only the space used by partitions instead of the whole
device.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_DD_BLOCKSIZE
Block size for dd.
Default: 1M.
.RB [ \-b ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_DD_PARMS
Additional dd parameters.
.RB [ \-D ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TAR_COMPRESSION_TOOL
Compression tool for compressed tar backups:
.BR bzip2 ,
.BR gzip ,
.BR lzip ,
.BR lzma ,
.BR lzop ,
.BR xz ,
.B zstd
or
.BR lz4 .
Ignored if
.B DEFAULT_ZIP_BACKUP
is enabled, which compresses with gzip.
.RB [ \-\-tarCompressionTool ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TAR_COMPRESSION_TOOL_OPTIONS
Options passed to the tar compression tool.
.RB [ \-\-tarCompressionToolOptions ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TAR_BOOT_PARTITION_ENABLED
Save the boot partition with tar instead of dd.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-B ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_LINK_BOOTPARTITIONFILES
Use hardlinks for identical boot partition backup files of consecutive
backups to save space.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_EXCLUDE_LIST
Additional excludes for tar and rsync.
Each exclude has to be prefixed with
.BR \-\-exclude ,
e.g.
.BR "\(dq\-\-exclude=/home/pi/.ssh \-\-exclude=/root/.ssh\(dq" .
.RB [ \-u ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_RSYNC_BACKUP_OPTION_EXCLUDE_ACLS
Don't save ACLs with rsync.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SKIPLOCALCHECK
Skip the check whether the backup path is a mounted partition.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-c ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_DYNAMIC_MOUNT
Partition (e.g.
.IR /dev/sda1 )
or mountpoint defined in
.I /etc/fstab
(e.g.
.IR /backup )
to mount before and unmount after the backup.
Empty disables dynamic mount.
.RB [ \-\-dynamicMount ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_REBOOT_SYSTEM
Reboot the system at the end of the backup.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-rebootSystem ]
.SH PARTITIONS
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PARTITIONBASED_BACKUP
Use partition oriented mode.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-P ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PARTITIONS_TO_BACKUP
Partitions to back up in partition oriented mode, e.g. \(dq1 2 5\(dq or
\(dq*\(dq for all.
Default: \(dq1 2\(dq.
.RB [ \-T ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PARTITIONS_TO_RESTORE
Partitions to restore from a partition oriented backup.
Default: \(dq1 2\(dq.
.RB [ \-T ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_IGNORE_ADDITIONAL_PARTITIONS
Ignore partitions with a number greater than 2 in normal mode.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-ignoreAdditionalPartitions ]
.SH BACKUP RETENTION
.TP
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS
Number of backups to keep.
Ignored if smart recycle is enabled.
Default: 3.
.RB [ \-k ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS_DD
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS_DDZ
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS_TAR
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS_TGZ
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS_RSYNC
Number of backups to keep per backup type.
0 means
.B DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS
is used.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-keep_dd ", " \-\-keep_ddz ", " \-\-keep_tar ", " \-\-keep_tgz ", " \-\-keep_rsync ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SMART_RECYCLE
Use the smart recycle strategy.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-smartRecycle ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SMART_RECYCLE_DRYRUN
Only report which backups smart recycle would delete.
Set to 0 to actually delete them.
Default: 1.
.RB [ \-\-smartRecycleDryrun ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SMART_RECYCLE_OPTIONS
Number of daily, weekly, monthly and yearly backups to keep.
Default: \(dq7 4 12 1\(dq.
.RB [ \-\-smartRecycleOptions ]
.SH SERVICES
.TP
.B DEFAULT_STOPSERVICES
Commands to stop services before the backup, separated by
.BR && .
\(dq:\(dq means no service has to be stopped.
.RB [ \-o ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_STARTSERVICES
Commands to start services after the backup, separated by
.BR && .
\(dq:\(dq means no service has to be started.
.RB [ \-a ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_BEFORE_STOPSERVICES
Commands to execute before the services are stopped, separated by
.BR && .
.TP
.B DEFAULT_AFTER_STARTSERVICES
Commands to execute after the services were started again, separated by
.BR && .
.SH RESTORE OPTIONS
.TP
.B DEFAULT_RESIZE_ROOTFS
Resize the root filesystem to the size of the restore device.
Default: 1.
.RB [ \-\-resizeRootFS ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_CHECK_FOR_BAD_BLOCKS
Check for bad blocks when formatting the restore device.
This takes a long time.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-C ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_RESTORE_REMINDER_INTERVAL
Remind to test a restore every this many months.
Default: 6.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_RESTORE_REMINDER_REPEAT
Number of times the restore reminder is repeated.
Default: 3.
.SH CLONE
.TP
.B DEFAULT_CLONE_DEVICE
Device to clone the system onto after the backup, e.g.
.I /dev/sda
or
.IR /dev/mmcblk0 .
.RB [ \-\-clone ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_CLONE_PARTUUID
PARTUUID of a partition of the clone device.
.SH EXTENSIONS
.TP
.B DEFAULT_EXTENSIONS
Space separated list of backup extensions to call.
.RB [ \-N ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_RESTORE_EXTENSIONS
Space separated list of restore extensions to call.
.SH MESSAGES AND LOGGING
.TP
.B DEFAULT_LANGUAGE
Message language:
.BR DE ,
.BR EN ,
.B FI
or
.BR FR .
Empty selects the system language.
.RB [ \-G ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_MSG_LEVEL
0 = minimal, 1 = detailed.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-m ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_LOG_OUTPUT
Location of the log file:
1 =
.RI /var/log/raspiBackup/ hostname .log ,
2 = backup directory,
3 = current directory,
or an absolute file name.
Default: 2.
.RB [ \-L ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_VERBOSE
Verbose output of the backup tools.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-v ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TIMESTAMPS
Prefix messages with timestamps.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-timestamps ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SYSTEMSTATUS
Write the system status into the debug log.
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-systemstatus ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_COLORING
Colorize console output
.RB ( C )
and/or eMails
.RB ( M ).
Default: CM.
.RB [ \-\-coloring ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_COLOR_CODES
HTML and VT100 color codes for warnings and errors.
Default: (\(dq#FF8000 33\(dq \(dq#FF0000 31\(dq).
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SKIP_DEPRECATED
Comma separated list of versions for which no deprecation message is
issued.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_OLD_REMINDER_REPEAT
How often to inform about backups with an old naming scheme.
Default: 5.
.SH EMAIL NOTIFICATION
.TP
.B DEFAULT_EMAIL
eMail address to send the completion status to.
Empty disables eMail notifications.
.RB [ \-e ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SENDER_EMAIL
Sender address used with ssmtp and msmtp.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_MAIL_PROGRAM
.BR mail ,
.BR ssmtp ,
.BR msmtp ,
.B sendEmail
or
.BR mailext .
Default: mail.
.RB [ \-s ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_EMAIL_PARMS
Additional parameters for the eMail program.
.RB [ \-E ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_EMAIL_COLORING
.B SUBJECT
or
.BR OPTION .
Default: SUBJECT.
.RB [ \-\-eMailColoring ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_MAIL_ON_ERROR_ONLY
Send eMails only in case of errors.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_NOTIFY_START
Also notify when the backup starts (eMail and Telegram).
Default: 0.
.RB [ \-\-notifyStart ]
.SH TELEGRAM NOTIFICATION
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TELEGRAM_TOKEN
Telegram bot token.
.RB [ \-\-telegramToken ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TELEGRAM_CHATID
Target chat id.
.RB [ \-\-telegramChatID ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TELEGRAM_THREADID
Thread id for threaded chats.
Empty means no thread is used.
.RB [ \-\-telegramThreadID ]
.TP
.B DEFAULT_TELEGRAM_NOTIFICATIONS
Notifications to send: any combination of
.B S
(success),
.B F
(failure),
.B M
(messages as file) and
.B m
(messages as text).
Default: F.
.RB [ \-\-telegramNotifications ]
.SH PUSHOVER NOTIFICATION
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_TOKEN
Pushover application token.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_USER
Pushover user key.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_DEVICE
Pushover device.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_NOTIFICATIONS
Notifications to send: any combination of
.B S
(success),
.B F
(failure) and
.B M
(messages).
Default: F.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_SOUND_SUCCESS
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_SOUND_FAILURE
Sound for success and failure notifications.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_PRIORITY_SUCCESS
.TQ
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_PRIORITY_FAILURE
Priority for success and failure notifications.
Default: 0 and 1.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_PUSHOVER_ADDITIONAL_OPTIONS
Additional API parameters, each prefixed with
.BR \-\-form\-string ,
e.g.
.BR "\(dq\-\-form\-string ttl=3600 \-\-form\-string priority=0\(dq" .
.SH SLACK NOTIFICATION
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL
Slack webhook URL.
.TP
.B DEFAULT_SLACK_NOTIFICATIONS
Notifications to send: any combination of
.B S
(success),
.B F
(failure) and
.B M
(messages).
.SH OBSOLETE OPTIONS
.TP
.B DEFAULT_DEPLOYMENT_HOSTS
Hosts which received the updated script with
.BR "raspiBackup \-y" .
Not used when raspiBackup is installed as Debian package.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
DEFAULT_BACKUPPATH="/backup"
DEFAULT_BACKUPTYPE="rsync"
DEFAULT_KEEPBACKUPS=5
DEFAULT_STOPSERVICES="systemctl stop nginx && systemctl stop mariadb"
DEFAULT_STARTSERVICES="systemctl start mariadb && systemctl start nginx"
DEFAULT_EMAIL="admin@example.com"
DEFAULT_MAIL_PROGRAM="msmtp"
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf
System wide configuration.
.TP
.I /usr/local/etc/raspiBackup.conf.bak
Previous configuration, saved by
.BR \-\-updateConfig .
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/raspibackup/raspiBackup_{en,de}.conf
Configuration templates with all options and their defaults.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR raspiBackup (1),
.BR raspiBackupInstallUI (1)
.PP
Full documentation:
.UR https://raspibackup.linux-tips-and-tricks.de/en/home/
.UE
